@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0127>
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:notation "dpp-0127" ;
  skos:prefLabel "lens"@eng ;
  skos:definition "profile conceived as a calibrated measuring instrument placed on the digital twin, which selects and transforms without altering the observed scene"@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "The mount — the profile interface on the neutral core — is the standardized element: any registered lens by any maker attaches to it."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "A lens publishes its calibration (version and cited rules), its uncertainty and its decision rules; it is subject to pattern approval at registration and to periodic re-verification through conformance runs."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Verification path-finds from any render through the lens and its fact chain to an anchor in the verifier's trust bundle."@eng
 .